      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-4,-4)$,$(-1,3)$,$(0,-1)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-4,-4)}=2-3(-4)(-4)=-46, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,3)}=2-3(-1)(3)=11, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,-1)}=2-3(0)(-1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/repairs/2026-10-20-early-cohort/jobs/17592186172038/workspace/evidence/assets/a23b59660071d64a34f11d39b61cd7b768ff81e004b408d7dbdfc459fb0b26ab.png)",
